Mutt: default color theme
Purpose: make Mutt Dark / Mutt Light (contributed by mutt-ai) the default color themes, so the app
  has its own visual identity out of the box. Only the setting *defaults* change: upstream's
  ThemeSettingDefaults (the fallback when a theme is missing) is untouched, so a build without
  mutt-ai falls back to the stock themes instead of an unstyled one.
Why not the extension API: an extension can't change another setting's default without also
  forcing it on every stock VS Code user of mutt-ai (Alpha), which we don't want.
Upstream files: src/vs/workbench/services/themes/common/themeConfiguration.ts

